// blaze, the trailer: exactly 60 seconds at 60 fps for X, landscape and upright from one scene. One flight: the
// camera never stops moving through a dark sea of points, and each idea is a landmark of light it nears, holds on and
// flies through (harness-video's src/backdrop.rs), with two to five words popping in and out under it. Three times
// the palette turns over (a field of the accent, dark type): the interrupts. Ideas, not metrics: what blaze is, then
// what it will be; speed is two beats. Every number is a row of data.json beside this file.
//
//   cd crates/harness
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film.mp4 x-landscape-1080p60        # the film, read back
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film-tall.mp4 x-portrait-1080x1920  # the same, upright
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sheet.png contact 0.5               # a frame each half second
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs burst.png burst 0.7                 # ten frames in a row
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs mix.wav                             # the mix alone
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sound.png sound                     # its waveform and spectrogram
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sounds                              # every sound event
//
// Cut to music: cuts.flecs places every beat on the track's grid (bar and beat), three acts: a cold open of hard
// cuts on single hits, a build whose cut rate doubles, the galaxy on the drop's downbeat, a montage, a break, the mark
// on the final downbeat and a button a bar later. The times below are with the temp score (104 beats a minute).
//
// Storyboard (cuts.flecs has the positions). Each beat: its landmark, its words, and what in the tree backs the claim.
//
//   at     beat      landmark (shot)             words                              backed by
//   0.00   cage      a hexagon nothing leaves    "build.rs: no network"             AGENTS.md rule 9 sandbox-everything; the sandbox
//                                                                                   refuses a script's network and stray writes
//   0.58   unclosed  INTERRUPT (accent field)    "unclosed file: compile error"     crates/hir-ty-linear/src/drops.rs:334 (CONSUME);
//                                                                                   blaze-std's File is `#[blaze::linear]`
//   1.15   check     a check mark, drawn         "90 theorems, in Lean"             lean/theorems.json (90 entries on main)
//   1.73   name      the sea; the galaxy, far    "blaze", "a compiler for agents"   AGENTS.md's first lines
//   4.62   agents    streams into a warm core    "agents, not keyboards"            the resident daemon and its API
//   6.92   rings     arcs that only narrow       "nothing ambient",                 crates/blaze-std/src/lib.rs:10-12 (capabilities
//                                                "capabilities only narrow"         made from an Io or by narrowing, never widened)
//   9.23   linear    INTERRUPT                   the compiler's error, verbatim     crates/hir-ty-linear/src/drops.rs:334
//   11.54  disk      a disk tears, time runs     "same code", "fake disk",          crates/blaze-core/src/sim.rs (blaze_core::sim::Sim;
//                    back, it tears again        "replays"                          the `testing` skill: seeded, replayable)
//   16.15  tree      a proof tree closing        "proved"                           lean/ (BlazeMir, BlazeValidated), theorems.json
//   18.47  prism     one beam, split             "pure", "nopanic", "noalloc"       104, 141 and 146 uses of the attributes in crates/
//   20.77  nopanic   INTERRUPT                   "#[blaze::nopanic]  v[i]",         the nopanic check's refusal ("a nopanic function and
//                                                "refused"                          everything it calls cannot panic or abort")
//   21.92  mirror    two builds read as one      "same bytes"                       AGENTS.md rule 25 deterministic-output
//   23.08  ripples   three rings to one shore    "no-op run", three names, times    data.json rows.noop (conditions on screen)
//   25.38  warp      the sea at speed            953.0 falling to 143.5, "body edit" data.json day.body
//   27.69  near      the galaxy, nearing         (no words)                         (the approach; the last beat before the drop is bare)
//   32.31  galaxy    THE PEAK, on the drop: dive  "one edit",                              docs/v2/plan/design/code-identity.md; rule 52
//                    it flares, four readers     "nothing compiled twice",          cache-by-code-id; the linker and live runtime
//                    light, nothing else stirs   "patched live"                     (docs/v2/plan/design/patch-in-place.md)
//   43.85  soon      comb, stair, store, cores   "soon": "the hub", "first-call     SOON: branches hub-1111, launcher-1111; the shared
//                                                compile", "shared store",          store and the scheduler for hundreds of cores are
//                                                "hundreds of cores"                designs (docs/v2/plan/design/scheduler.md)
//   53.08  quiet     the sea alone; silence      "blaze builds blaze"               AGENTS.md rule 2 (blaze builds blaze as the proof)
//   55.38  end       the sea streams in          the mark, the repository
//
// The open loop: the galaxy is in the sky behind the name at 2.25 s, small; the film arrives in it on the drop.
// Honesty: a claim on screen is something the tree has, or is under the "soon" tag. The one comparison is a measured
// row, drawn to scale (each ring's time to the shore is its share of the slowest's), its conditions passing once.
// Sound: the track, with the beats' own synthesised events under it (`harness-video ... sounds` lists them): a hit on
// each opening cut, a rise into the edit's one big hit, and the track's one silence before the last line.
include cuts
include tokens
include parts
include open
include today
include speed
include galaxy
include soon
include end

@tree ChildOf
film : ui.ZStack {
  Video: {width: 960, height: 540, fps: 60, seconds: $t_out, scale: 2, reframes: true}
  // The picture: which landmark and its numbers are cued by each beat.
  Backdrop: {shot: 0, at: 0, a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, d: 0, e: 0, f: 1}
  // -16 LUFS integrated, no true peak over -1 dBTP: loud enough on a phone, with headroom for X's re-encode.
  Mix: {lufs: -16, peak: -1}
  Flex: {axis: Z, gap: 0, align: Center, justify: Center, wrap: false}
  Size: {w: {kind: Fixed, value: 960, min: 0, max: 0}, h: {kind: Fixed, value: 540, min: 0, max: 0}}
  // The film is cut to a track: music.wav beside this file (not in the tree: the owner's file, or the temp score
  // `harness-video score` writes), its grid in beats.json. The beats' own sounds sit under it.
  Music: {gain: 1.0, under: 0.55}
}
